# Machine-local judge-call cache. Demonstrated able to silently hold a wrong,
# confident answer (109/169 entries once cached SAFE for 429 error text,
# results.md S1.5) - sharing it between machines/sessions means a "verdict"
# in someone's results could actually be a stale or poisoned cache hit from
# a different machine's history, with no way to tell. Guards now prevent new
# error-text poisoning (semantic.py cache_get/cache_set), but the file stays
# local-only rebuildable scratch state, not something to commit.
backend/app/evaluation/semantic_cache.json
